[node name="Lbl_TitleGeneral" type="RichTextLabel" parent="MainLayout/ContentStage/Panel_Guidebook/VBox/ScrollContainer/ScrollVbox"]
custom_minimum_size = Vector2(0, 64)
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 3
size_flags_vertical = 4
theme_override_colors/font_outline_color = Color(0, 0, 0, 1)
theme_override_constants/outline_size = 24
theme_override_fonts/normal_font = ExtResource("3_yx35g")
theme_override_fonts/bold_font = ExtResource("3_yx35g")
theme_override_font_sizes/normal_font_size = 42
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "Ballomachy General Tips and Tricks
"
horizontal_alignment = 1

[node name="Lbl_ExplanationGeneral" type="RichTextLabel" parent="MainLayout/ContentStage/Panel_Guidebook/VBox/ScrollContainer/ScrollVbox"]
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 3
size_flags_vertical = 3
theme_override_colors/font_outline_color = Color(0, 0, 0, 1)
theme_override_constants/outline_size = 24
theme_override_constants/line_separation = 8
theme_override_fonts/normal_font = ExtResource("3_yx35g")
theme_override_font_sizes/normal_font_size = 42
text = "
So, you're ass at ballomachy?

It's a tough game, but you're in the right hands!

First things First: The Basics

Reach the target score before your opponent, or face certain death!

There are 4 quarters with 7 games each, with a boss at the end of each quarter offering incalculable rewards!

You'll gain threads throughout the games that will help you conquer the increasing difficulty. See threads for more info!


Gain \"Mach\" by styling on your opponent!

Mach Can be generated in the following ways:

*Steals
*Blocks
*Dunks
*3pters
*Thread modifiers
*Bait Manipulation
*Bulldozing the opponent to the dirt!

Your Max Mach Multiplier is 4, but can be raised or lowered in various ways!

After each game, you'll gain an attribute bonus equal to 1 times your mach multiplier.

e.g. ending mach 3, +3 to all stats!

If you ever turn the ball over, that's a big no-no. Your MachMultiplier will reset!

Now, with the basics out of the way, go out there and tear it up, we're all counting on you!





"

[node name="Lbl_TitleThreads" type="RichTextLabel" parent="MainLayout/ContentStage/Panel_Guidebook/VBox/ScrollContainer/ScrollVbox"]
visible = false
custom_minimum_size = Vector2(0, 64)
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 3
size_flags_vertical = 4
theme_override_colors/font_outline_color = Color(0, 0, 0, 1)
theme_override_constants/outline_size = 24
theme_override_fonts/normal_font = ExtResource("3_yx35g")
theme_override_font_sizes/normal_font_size = 42
text = "Threads, your stylish counterpart
"
horizontal_alignment = 1

[node name="Lbl_ExplanationThreads" type="RichTextLabel" parent="MainLayout/ContentStage/Panel_Guidebook/VBox/ScrollContainer/ScrollVbox"]
visible = false
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 3
size_flags_vertical = 3
theme_override_colors/font_outline_color = Color(0, 0, 0, 1)
theme_override_constants/outline_size = 24
theme_override_constants/line_separation = 8
theme_override_fonts/normal_font = ExtResource("3_yx35g")
theme_override_font_sizes/normal_font_size = 42
text = "Depending on your class/difficulty, you'll have empty thread slots that can be filled with threads you'll acquire after defeating opponents.

In most cases you will have:
*A left/Right arm slot
*A left/Right Shoe Slot
*An outfit slot
*A head slot for headgear
*A ball Slot


Utilize these slots and roll with the punches to have your best chance of reaching cronus!

Some Threads give you flat bonuses to things like your 3pt, your speed, etc.

Some Threads are purely utility, like increasing the shot clock, or raising your maximum MachMultiplier.

There's a wide variety of threads you'll encounter throughout the run.


Depending on your class/Difficulty, you'll have storage slots in the locker room where you can store your extra threads if you ever want to swap them out, or even better: Make useless ones use-ful!

See the Locker Room for info on the Altar!


Don't worry about trying to find a perfect thread to go with your build! 

It's randomized, not intentionally annoying, and if you lean into what's given, you'll forget you even had to read this tutorial!

Last Note: Threads are only obtained at the end of games, I assure you. 

Now ball, with styyyylllleee!



"

[node name="Lbl_TitleBait" type="RichTextLabel" parent="MainLayout/ContentStage/Panel_Guidebook/VBox/ScrollContainer/ScrollVbox"]
visible = false
custom_minimum_size = Vector2(0, 64)
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 3
size_flags_vertical = 4
theme_override_colors/font_outline_color = Color(0, 0, 0, 1)
theme_override_constants/outline_size = 24
theme_override_fonts/normal_font = ExtResource("3_yx35g")
theme_override_font_sizes/normal_font_size = 42
text = "Bait, you know you want it!
"
horizontal_alignment = 1

[node name="Lbl_ExplanationBait" type="RichTextLabel" parent="MainLayout/ContentStage/Panel_Guidebook/VBox/ScrollContainer/ScrollVbox"]
visible = false
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 3
size_flags_vertical = 3
theme_override_colors/font_outline_color = Color(0, 0, 0, 1)
theme_override_constants/outline_size = 24
theme_override_constants/line_separation = 8
theme_override_fonts/normal_font = ExtResource("3_yx35g")
theme_override_font_sizes/normal_font_size = 42
text = "Bait can be acquired from the Oceanus Bait Shop, and is mighty tempting.

Baits cost energy (See locker room) and come with both a catch and a hook.


Each bait has a positive that is hard to ignore and a drawback that you can see at any point on your clipboard!

The duration for each bait varies, but the types of duration are consistent.


Certain bait will be permanent, like stat buffs and drawbacks that are instantly realized and never go away!

Others (and most of them) have an expiration time where you will lose the debuff.

Not all Hooks Expire, but most of them are simple short-Term helpers that will fade away.

No fun! Well at least the curse goes away too!

Every Locker Room visit will refresh the bait shop and you can peruse it any time you feel.

The only cost is for buying them with your limited energy you get every locker Room visit.


I'm not a salesman for Oceanus, but give it a try and you may find it can help give you the edge or help you lean into your build more!

See ya at the shop!
"

